    3.5 Humanitarian Assistance
    This report presents data on the population characteristics, literacy, educational attainment, migration,
    economic activity, functional difficulty, fertility, mortality, birth registration and living status of parents, The SDES includes a mapping and listing of all houses, business establishments and institutions
    disaggregated by sex and district. Information on the household and housing characteristics is also at the district and village levels as well as the location of community infrastructure, such as health
    included. The findings of the report will aid the development planners and programme implementers facilities, schools, mosques, markets and roads, which is essential for emergency preparedness plans
    to come up with sound policies and programmes designed for the localities for the effective delivery of to mitigate the effects of disaster. Population groups are categorized by sex, age, education, literacy,
    basic services to the people of Afghanistan. employment status and other important variables which can help shape humanitarian assistance if it
    should be needed.
    To ensure that high quality data are collected in SDES, several layers of supervision and monitoring
    were included, from the training of surveyors to survey enumeration and data processing. 3.6 Research
