    SAMANGAN SOCIO-DEMOGRAPHIC AND ECONOMIC SURVEY
    4.2 Survey Enumeration 7. POPULATION
    Unlike previous CSO surveys, which were designed to provide data at the provincial level, SDES focuses CHARACTERISTICS
    on district and even smaller units, including urban subdivisions, major villages and clusters of small
    villages. This will prove valuable for local development planning and for monitoring public service delivery.
    The first step in the survey was to list every household in each village. Half of these listed households (i.e.
    7.1 Population Distribution by District
    every other household) were taken as samples and asked detailed questions.
    Aybak, the provincial centre, had the largest population in Samangan, comprising 29.4 percent of
    the total population in the province. Dara-e-Soof-e-Payin had the second-largest population with
    5. MONITORING AND SUPERVISION
